window.docContents[173].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Process.Loader/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Process___Loader":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Process › Loader.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the symbolic proof 5 headline theorems depend on it 468 of 540 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nDeclarations on this page (23)def listGetBytedef listReadU16LEdef listReadU32LEdef listReadU64LEdef pageAlignDowndef pageAlignUpdef alignUp16def insertRegionSorteddef regionAlignedValiddef regionsDisjointAndAligneddef entryInExecRegiondef ElfImage.WellFormeddef parseProgramHeaderdef parseProgramHeadersdef readStrtabCStringdef parseSymtabEntriesdef findSymtabShdrdef parseSymtabdef ElfImage.parsedef packCStringListdef buildInitialStackdef initFsStatedef ElfImage.loadState\n\nStatic ELF64 Loader & Linux AArch64 Initial Process State (Arm64.Trusted.Process.Loader)* Layer / Role: Arm64 Trusted Computing Base (Role::Spec, definitions only, 0 theorems).* Purpose & Key Exports: Pure-Lean static ELF64 ET_EXEC parser (ElfImage.parse, including SHT_SYMTAB/SHT_STRTAB function symbol extraction), well-formedness check (ElfImage.WellFormed), deterministic Linux AArch64 initial stack/auxiliary-vector builder (buildInitialStack), initial file-descriptor and in-memory file-system setup (initFsState), process state loader (ElfImage.loadState, loadElf).* When to read: Read when auditing how a statically linked ELF64 binary is validated and mapped into an initial Arm64.State (PT_LOAD segments, SHT_SYMTAB symbols, brkStart, argc/argv/envp/auxv on the stack, and fd 0/1/2 in State.fs).\n\n\n\nLittle-Endian Byte Readers for ELF64 Parsing\n\ndef listGetByteL36–40 ↗#Read byte off of bs : List (BitVec 8) as a Nat (0 if out of bounds).\n\ndef listReadU16LEL42–47 ↗#Read a 16-bit little-endian unsigned integer from bs : List (BitVec 8) at byte offset off.\n\ndef listReadU32LEL49–54 ↗#Read a 32-bit little-endian unsigned integer from bs : List (BitVec 8) at byte offset off.\n\ndef listReadU64LEL56–62 ↗#Read a 64-bit little-endian unsigned integer from bs : List (BitVec 8) at byte offset off.\n\ndef pageAlignDownL64–66 ↗#Round n down to a multiple of Obj.pageSize (4096).\n\ndef pageAlignUpL68–70 ↗#Round n up to a multiple of Obj.pageSize (4096).\n\ndef alignUp16L72–74 ↗#Round n up to a multiple of 16.\n\nPure-Lean ELF64 ET_EXEC Parser (ElfImage.parse)\n\ndef insertRegionSortedL78–83 ↗#Insert a Snapshot.Region into a list ordered by ascending start.toNat.\n\ndef regionAlignedValidL85–95 ↗#Check that a single region is page-aligned, non-empty, within 48-bit user address space, mapped, and W^X compliant.\n\ndef regionsDisjointAndAlignedL97–104 ↗#Check that adjacent regions in a sorted list are strictly non-overlapping and page-aligned.\n\ndef entryInExecRegionL106–112 ↗#Check that entry is 4-byte aligned and lies within an executable (perm.x) region.\n\ndef ElfImage.WellFormedL114–121 ↗#Structural well-formedness check on a parsed ElfImage.\n\ndef parseProgramHeaderL123–210 ↗#Parse a single 56-byte ELF64 program header ph over bytes : List (BitVec 8) of length fileSize. Fails closed on PT_INTERP, PT_DYNAMIC, executable PT_GNU_STACK, W+X segments, or unknown segment types.\n\ndef parseProgramHeadersL212–220 ↗#Parse ePhnum 56-byte program headers from phTable.\n\ndef readStrtabCStringL222–230 ↗#Read a NUL-terminated string from bs within rem remaining bytes of .strtab.\n\ndef parseSymtabEntriesL232–255 ↗#Walk numEntries 24-byte ELF64 SHT_SYMTAB entries by structural recursion on numEntries, extracting defined STT_FUNC ((st_info &&& 0xf) == 2, st_shndx != 0, st_name != 0) symbols (name, vaddr).\n\ndef findSymtabShdrL257–266 ↗#Scan eShnum 64-byte section headers in shTable for SHT_SYMTAB (sh_type == 2), returning some (shOffset, shSize, shLink, shInfo, shEntsize).\n\ndef parseSymtabL268–305 ↗#Extract defined STT_FUNC symbols from SHT_SYMTAB / SHT_STRTAB in bytes : List (BitVec 8).\n\ndef ElfImage.parseL307–359 ↗#Parse a raw ELF64 ET_EXEC AArch64 binary (List (BitVec 8)) into an ElfImage. References:* System V ABI (ELF-64 Object File Format): https://refspecs.linuxfoundation.org/elf/gabi4+/contents.html* ELF for the Arm 64-bit Architecture (AAELF64): https://github.com/ARM-software/abi-aa/blob/main/aaelf64/aaelf64.rst\n\nDeterministic Linux AArch64 Initial Stack & Auxiliary Vector Construction\n\ndef packCStringListL363–372 ↗#Pack a list of NUL-terminated byte strings into a flat byte buffer starting at baseAddr, returning (endOffset, flatBytes, stringAddresses).\n\ndef buildInitialStackL374–466 ↗#Construct the initial Linux AArch64 user stack frame ([sp, stackTop)) for img and inputs (following Linux fs/exec.c bprm_mm_init + fs/binfmt_elf.c create_elf_tables and QEMU linux-user/elfload.c setup_arg_pages + create_elf_tables):* Top of stack ([infoBase, stackTop)): 16-byte AT_RANDOM buffer at 16-byte-aligned infoBase, < 16 zero alignment bytes, \"aarch64\\0\" platform string (AT_PLATFORM), NUL-terminated argv strings, NUL-terminated envp strings, NUL-terminated inputs.execfn string (AT_EXECFN), and the 8-byte top-of-stack zero sentinel word (sizeof(void *)).* Frame table ([sp, infoBase)): argc, argv[0..argc-1], NULL, envp[0..envc-1], NULL, and auxv (a_type, a_val) pairs ending with (AT_NULL, 0), padded to 16-byte alignment so sp % 16 == 0.\n\nInitial File-System & Standard-Stream State (initFsState)\n\ndef initFsStateL470–488 ↗#Construct the initial FsState from inputs:* fd 0 is open .rdonly (kind := .stdio) at offset 0 backed by fs.stdin = inputs.stdin;* fd 1 and fd 2 are open .wronly (kind := .stdio) streams;* entries contains only CWD ([] = .dir), non-empty path prefixes of inputs.dirs, strict ancestor prefixes of inputs.files, and each (p, bs) in inputs.files under normalizePath p (standard streams never pollute the CWD file namespace).\n\nProcess State Loader (ElfImage.loadState, loadElf)\n\ndef ElfImage.loadStateL492–533 ↗#Load a validated ElfImage with inputs into its initial Arm64.State:* Rejects any inputs.dirs or inputs.files path with a leading '/' or \"..\" segment, or any initial regular file exceeding MAX_LFS_FILESIZE (2 ^ 63 - 1), fail-closed (Except.error).* All PT_LOAD segments and the populated stack frame [sp, stackTop) are mapped via Snapshot.cellAt, and the remaining stack [stackTop - stackSize, sp) is mapped zero-filled Perm.rw via Memory.mapZero.* pc = img.entry, sp is the 16-byte-aligned initial stack pointer, regs and vregs are zeroed (ELF_PLAT_INIT), brkStart = brk = img.brkStart, physMemAvail = inputs.init.physMemAvail, fs = initFsState inputs, and oracle = inputs.init.oracle.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 535–538): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesArm64.Process.loadElf\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Process/Loader.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Process.Loader/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Process___Loader"}});